course: dictionary
lesson: 12339
title: Covertly: doing things in secret
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something is done. Covertly is one of them. It tells you that someone does a thing in secret, so that others do not notice. Look at the action word next to it, then ask: was this done in a hidden way?
explain: «The spy covertly passed the map to her friend under the table.» The clue is under the table: the spy hides what she is doing. So covertly means in a secret way, out of sight. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The spy secretly passed the map" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Covertly can also describe a feeling that is kept hidden. «She was covertly unhappy, but she smiled all day.» Nobody could see her sadness, so it was hidden. The opposite is «openly», which means in plain view: «He openly said he was cross.»
fact: Covertly is an adverb, a word that tells how an action is done.
fact: «Covertly» means in a secret or hidden way, so that others do not notice.
fact: «Covertly» can also mean not openly shown or admitted, as in «covertly unhappy».
fact: The opposite of covertly is «openly», which means in plain view or out in the open.
fact: Spy stories, mysteries and news about secret agents or police often use covertly.
exercise: «The agent covertly followed the thief through the crowd.» What does covertly mean? | Loudly and proudly | *In a secret way, so no one notices | Very quickly, shouting for help | Slowly, with a big smile
exercise: Maya covertly slipped a note to her friend during maths. Which word means the opposite of covertly? | secretly | slyly | silently | *openly
exercise: Which sentence shows someone acting covertly? | *He tiptoed in and took a biscuit while no one was watching. | The sun rose slowly over the hills. | She shouted her answer across the room. | They cheered loudly at the football match.
test: «The detective covertly watched the house from her car.» Covertly here means: | *Secretly, so the people inside could not see her | Very noisily | Openly, in full view of everyone | Happily, with music playing
test: Sam covertly looked at his friend's answers. What does covertly tell us? | He did it in front of the whole class | *He did it in secret | He did it very loudly | He did it because the teacher asked him to
exam: «She covertly sent a message to the spy by hiding it inside a book.» Which word is closest in meaning to covertly? | openly | *secretly | loudly | proudly
